From: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 08:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: skip idle check on no-TZ suspend

QCS6490 quirk: booted via the no-TZ path (KODIAKWP firmware), the VPU
firmware does not reliably report WFI/idle at session teardown, so the
readx_poll_timeout(venus_cpu_and_video_core_idle, ...) in
venus_suspend_3xx() intermittently times out (-ETIMEDOUT) and wedges
the VPU until reboot ("wait for cpu and video core idle fail (-110)";
every later session fails).

The power-collapse and resume path itself is proven on this board, so
skip the idle check on no-TZ systems and collapse unconditionally.
This matches the older venus_suspend_1xx flow, which has no idle
handshake at all.

Signed-off-by: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
index d3da35f..e024cb4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
@@ -1604,6 +1604,18 @@ static int venus_suspend_3xx(struct venus_core *core)
 	if (ctrl_status & CPU_CS_SCIACMDARG0_PC_READY)
 		goto power_off;
 
+	/*
+	 * QCS6490 quirk: booted via the no-TZ path (KODIAKWP firmware),
+	 * the VPU firmware does not reliably report WFI/idle at session
+	 * teardown, so this poll intermittently times out (-ETIMEDOUT)
+	 * and wedges the VPU until reboot. The power-collapse and resume
+	 * path itself is proven on this board, so skip the idle check on
+	 * no-TZ systems and collapse unconditionally (matches the older
+	 * venus_suspend_1xx flow, which has no idle handshake at all).
+	 */
+	if (!core->use_tz)
+		goto power_off;
+
 	/*
 	 * Power collapse sequence for Venus 3xx and 4xx versions:
 	 * 1. Check for ARM9 and video core to be idle by checking WFI bit
-- 
